{"name":"Santiago Orange","hex":"#e95f24","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree.\n Specifically, a sweet orange or Citrus sinensis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"}],"entries":[{"title":"Santiago","blocks":[{"text":"Santiago, also known as Santiago de Chile, is the capital and largest city of Chile and one of the largest cities in the Americas. Located in the Chilean Central Valley within the Santiago Basin, between the Andes to the east and the Chilean Coastal Range to the west, it anchors the Santiago Metropolitan Region and its conurbation of Greater Santiago, which comprises more than forty communes and concentrates over a third of the national population and around 45% of Chile's GDP. Most of the city lies between 500 and 650 meters above sea level, with recent urban growth extending into the Andean foothills."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Palacio_de_La_Moneda_-_miguelreflex.jpg/330px-Palacio_de_La_Moneda_-_miguelreflex.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santiago"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Santiago_de_Chile%2C_Desde_Cerro_San_Crist%C3%B3bal_%28cropped_panorama%29.jpg/500px-Santiago_de_Chile%2C_Desde_Cerro_San_Crist%C3%B3bal_%28cropped_panorama%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Santiago_de_Chile%2C_Desde_Cerro_San_Crist%C3%B3bal_%28cropped_panorama%29.jpg/1280px-Santiago_de_Chile%2C_Desde_Cerro_San_Crist%C3%B3bal_%28cropped_panorama%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Santiago_de_Chile%2C_Desde_Cerro_San_Crist%C3%B3bal_%28cropped_panorama%29.jpg/500px-Santiago_de_Chile%2C_Desde_Cerro_San_Crist%C3%B3bal_%28cropped_panorama%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASantiago_de_Chile%2C_Desde_Cerro_San_Crist%C3%B3bal_(cropped_panorama).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Biblioteca_Nacional_de_Chile%2C_2012-09-08.jpg/500px-Biblioteca_Nacional_de_Chile%2C_2012-09-08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Biblioteca_Nacional_de_Chile%2C_2012-09-08.jpg/1280px-Biblioteca_Nacional_de_Chile%2C_2012-09-08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Biblioteca_Nacional_de_Chile%2C_2012-09-08.jpg/500px-Biblioteca_Nacional_de_Chile%2C_2012-09-08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fi